    <unit id="4" name="PageSubtitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Customize AtomUI themes with Global Tokens, algorithms, Control Tokens, and nested local theme scopes.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="5" name="PageDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Customize Theme demonstrates how ThemeConfigProvider overrides Global Tokens, applies preset algorithms, configures Control Tokens, and nests theme contexts without changing the global application theme.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="6" name="ApiMemberThemeConfigProviderConfig">
      <segment>
        <source>Immutable scoped theme configuration. Runtime updates replace the complete value.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="7" name="ApiMemberThemeConfigInherit">
      <segment>
        <source>Whether this configuration inherits and merges the parent theme configuration.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="8" name="ApiMemberThemeConfigAlgorithms">
      <segment>
        <source>Ordered ThemeAlgorithm values. A null value inherits the parent algorithm chain.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="9" name="ApiMemberThemeConfigTokens">
      <segment>
        <source>Global token overrides keyed by token name.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="10" name="ApiMemberThemeConfigControls">
      <segment>
        <source>Control theme configurations keyed by ControlTokenIdentity.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="11" name="ApiMemberControlThemeConfigAlgorithm">
      <segment>
        <source>How the control applies algorithms: Unspecified, Disabled, Global, or Custom.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="12" name="ApiMemberControlThemeConfigAlgorithms">
      <segment>
        <source>Ordered ThemeAlgorithm values used only when Algorithm is Custom.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="13" name="ApiMemberControlThemeConfigTokens">
      <segment>
        <source>Global Token and Own Token overrides applied only to the selected Control identity.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="14" name="CustomizeDesignTokenTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Customize Design Token</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="15" name="CustomizeDesignTokenDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>By modifying token property of theme, we can modify Design Token globally. Some tokens will affect other tokens. We call these tokens Seed Token.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="16" name="PresetAlgorithmsTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Use Preset Algorithms</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="17" name="PresetAlgorithmsDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Themes with different styles can be quickly generated by modifying algorithm. Ant Design 5.0 provides three sets of preset algorithms by default: DefaultAlgorithm, DarkAlgorithm, CompactAlgorithm.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="18" name="RuntimeTokenUpdatesTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Runtime Token Updates</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="19" name="RuntimeTokenUpdatesDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Replace ThemeConfigProvider.Config with a new immutable ThemeConfig to publish one scoped snapshot without adding resource provider layers.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="20" name="CustomizeControlTokenTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Customize Control Tokens</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="21" name="CustomizeControlTokenDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Every publicly themeable Control has an independent identity. Its configuration can override any Global Token and that Control's Own Tokens; the overrides affect only the selected Control and do not leak to other Controls.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="22" name="NestedThemeTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Nested Theme</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="23" name="NestedThemeDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>By nesting ConfigProvider you can apply a local theme to part of your page. Design Tokens that are not changed in the child theme inherit from the parent theme.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
